The model of Mica has no language setting. A site in several languages uses one of two patterns. Both work with the current version and need no extra code in Mica.

| Pattern | Use it for | Limits |
| --- | --- | --- |
| One field per language | Pages and settings that exist in each language. | The form shows all languages. |
| One collection per language | News or other content that is different in each language. | The editor does not connect a text with its translation. |

## One field per language

Put the languages in an `object()`. The translations of a page stay in one entry, so they do not drift apart.

```ts
import { collection, object, richText, slug, text } from "@micacms/core";

pages: collection({
  label: "Pages",
  fields: {
    // The slug of the entry: the same for each language.
    slug: slug(),
    title: object({ label: "Title", fields: { de: text({ label: "Deutsch", required: true }), en: text({ label: "English" }) } }),
    body: object({ label: "Text", fields: { de: richText({ label: "Deutsch" }), en: richText({ label: "English" }) } }),
    // A URL for each language, when the URLs must differ.
    url: object({ label: "URL", fields: { de: slug({ label: "Deutsch" }), en: slug({ label: "English" }) } }),
  },
}),
```

Mica stores the text in `index.json` and the rich text in one file for each language:

```text
content/pages/about/index.json   { "title": { "de": "Über uns", "en": "About us" }, "url": { "de": "ueber-uns", "en": "about-us" } }
content/pages/about/body.de.mdoc
content/pages/about/body.en.mdoc
```

The slug of an entry is unique, because it is the name of its folder. A URL in the `url` object is not checked: neither `npx mica check` nor Astro finds two pages with the same English URL, and Astro then builds only one of them. Keep these URLs unique.

### Alt text in several languages

`media({ alt })` holds one alt text. Keep `media()` without `alt`, and put an object for the alt text next to it:

```ts
image: media({ label: "Image", accept: "image" }),
imageAlt: object({ label: "Alt text", fields: { de: text({ label: "Deutsch" }), en: text({ label: "English" }) } }),
```

### The pages

Tell Astro the languages in `astro.config.mjs`. With `prefixDefaultLocale`, each language has its prefix, also the default one (`/de/…`), as the page below expects:

```js
export default defineConfig({
  i18n: { locales: ["de", "en"], defaultLocale: "de", routing: { prefixDefaultLocale: true } },
});
```

Make one page for each entry and language, for example in `src/pages/[lang]/[slug].astro`:

```astro
---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import { renderRichText } from "@micacms/astro";

export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const pages = await getCollection("pages");
  return (["de", "en"] as const).flatMap((lang) =>
    pages.map((page) => ({ params: { lang, slug: page.data.url?.[lang] ?? page.id }, props: { page, lang } })),
  );
}

const { page, lang } = Astro.props;
const body = await renderRichText(page.data.body?.[lang], page.data);
---
<h1>{page.data.title[lang] ?? page.data.title.de}</h1>
<Fragment set:html={body} />
```

A missing translation shows the default language here. Choose what your site does: show the default language, or make no page.

## One collection per language

Give each language its own collection:

```ts
newsDe: collection({ label: "News (Deutsch)", fields: { title: text({ required: true }), slug: slug({ from: "title" }), body: richText() } }),
newsEn: collection({ label: "News (English)", fields: { title: text({ required: true }), slug: slug({ from: "title" }), body: richText() } }),
```

Each collection is a list of its own in the editor, with its own folder, URLs and order. When a text has a translation, a `relation()` field can name it.

## Later versions

A later version of Mica can add a `localized` option. Mica's decisions fix its storage now: it stores what the first pattern stores today, `body.de.mdoc` included. A site that uses the first pattern can then change to the option with no change to its files. See the decision "No native multilingual content in 1.0" in [decisions.md](https://github.com/micacms/mica/blob/main/docs/decisions.md).
